  "description": "Foreign keys that may have no index the referential check can use (DBP-1.12, #7195). test/foreign-key-index-coverage.test.ts fails when a foreign key without a usable index is missing from this list, and when a listed one is now indexed or no longer exists. Add an entry only with a reason from `reasons`; prefer indexing the column (a partial index WHERE <col> IS NOT NULL for a sparse nullable column).",
